editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-38.md:109:"I've one rule at this table that I never taught anybody, since I'd not have thought it wanted teaching. Nobody lies down here without being told what I'm going to do to them, and why, and what it's like to cost. I tell a child. I tell a man who's out of his head with a fever, and I say it twice, in case one of the times gets in." She nodded at the plank. "You lay down there this morning knowing what you were going to do to me. The one person in this room who wasn't told was the healer. You turned my table round. That's what you did, and I'll thank you not to dress it."
