+| Opening pull | Ch. 38, opening table confession through “I opened it” (line 37), then Oryn’s “You turned my table round” (line 109) | **8/10, high confidence.** The secrecy, tenth power, and immediate accusation give a strong problem, though nine named fragments and several past locations arrive before a new reader can sort them. | **9/10, high confidence.** The consent problem converts exposition into confrontation, and the physical intimacy of the examination sharpens it. |
+| Keep reading | Ch. 38, “It was mine to say” (line 153); Ch. 40, the unmoving place all ten currents avoid (around line 347); Ch. 44, “Tomorrow makes three” (line 217) | **8/10, high confidence.** Several questions remain alive and each chapter pays something off, especially the power training and shooting. The research run delays the outward next move. | **9/10, high confidence.** Ethical, bodily, institutional, and archaeological pressures converge without collapsing into one answer. |
+| Interest / freshness | Ch. 39, Cael hearing his fragments as grass, millstone, wick, bellows, nail, glass, silence, and sea; Ch. 41, Karis applying the apple lesson to one archaeological site | **9/10, high confidence.** Powers become sensory and trainable, while research is made concrete with barley, bark, rubbings, and apples. | **9/10, high confidence.** The movement’s unusual center is disciplined observation rather than revelation, and character habits generate the method. |
+| Clarity / flow | Ch. 41, noon on day 104 (line 65) followed later by the night of day 103 (line 125); all four unresolved insertions | **6/10, high confidence.** Scene-level action is clear, but the backward date jump, dense proper nouns, and literal editorial tokens create avoidable rereading. | **7/10, high confidence.** Causal logic is strong, but chronology briefly tangles and the repeated distinction among observation, finding, hypothesis, and fear slows the line. |
+| Character attachment | Ch. 40, Lira’s “It’s still your day” (line 63) and the nineteenth birthday; Ch. 43, Oryn finding the eighth mend has taken (line 135); Ch. 44, Oryn repeatedly reaching for the absent cheek-strap | **9/10, high confidence.** Care is shown through actions and limits rather than speeches, and each crew member contributes differently. | **10/10, high confidence.** Oryn’s anger and care coexist without cancellation; Lira’s pride, Brom’s plain loyalty, Karis’s rigor, and Seln’s restraint remain sharply individual. |
